From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wmic: aliases, WHERE, GET/LIST/CALL, the table, list, value and csv formats, /OUTPUT, /APPEND, /NAMESPACE

wmic answered only "<alias> get <properties>" with equal-width columns. It now has the alias list (80 aliases and their classes), "path" and "class", WHERE clauses as typed (a quoted clause, a clause with LIKE), GET with properties, LIST BRIEF/FULL, CALL with positional or named parameters on one class or on every instance WHERE selects, with Windows' output ("Executing ...", "Method execution successful.", "Out Parameters: instance of __PARAMETERS"), /FORMAT:TABLE|LIST|CSV|VALUE and /VALUE, columns in property-name order each as wide as its own values, booleans as TRUE/FALSE, arrays as {"a", "b"}, /OUTPUT:file|CLIPBOARD|NUL and /APPEND (a Unicode file with a byte order mark), /NAMESPACE, /NODE (this machine only), "No Instance(s) Available.", Invalid GET Expression, WMI errors with their code, facility and text. wbemprox: method names match in any case; IWbemClassObject::Next lists the system properties first (flags select, as GetNames does); a WHERE on a property the class lacks is an invalid query.
